# === dsh-deepartments patch: dsh CLI profile-boot watchUserPatchLayers (R3) ===
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES
#   The dsh CLI profile-boot watched only the profile + home patch files with
#   two watchUserPatches calls. This patch switches it to ONE
#   watchUserPatchLayers call over bundle layers (required) + profile + home,
#   with the live composition rebuilt from the watcher's re-read layers.
#   ADAPTATIONS to rc.2 (skew): the runtime chunk lacks the upstream
#   patchReload gate / installProxyFromEnvironment / createAppReady / async
#   composeProfile / agent-presets removal — those are upstream drift AFTER
#   rc.2 and are intentionally NOT ported; the payload hunks were applied onto
#   the runtime chunk as-is (import, composeLive, watchUserPatchLayers call).
#   The chunk name is a build hash (profile-boot-<hash>.js): the reapply
#   variant locates the real chunk by content.
#
# TARGET FILE
#   <npm-root>/@deepseek-ai/dsh/lib/profile-boot-DG5t9aNs.js
#   (the live chunk filename; after dsh upgrades re-locate by content)
#
# FINGERPRINTS (md5)
#  12f9ba5a4400a8e795f1d72254119ffb  pristine rc.2 chunk
#  c359a2f3cb7d912b38bc1c2eb14b40a1  patched (this patch applied)
#
